  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_1fa7b469a4a341a483fe1a1fc0ed5014",
      "statement": "The backend money model uses two representations: raw numeric values (prices, position quantity and average_cost) are `Decimal` in the API types, while any currency-tagged amount is `stockholm.Money`, and `Account.currency` / `Security.currency` are `stockholm.currency.Currency` rather than plain strings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/account/api_types.py#L1-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be5e23cd0fdf4b5700521db06c68c6de1ab6af43b02dd98dbcf9338f01120b93:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/account/schema.py#L26-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7e1e0142047e4f3818eaa037fa317adf6128d2c1ffa3b5a11f6bbf76a9231d3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/market/api_types.py#L13-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6041a79f4d88273c8a57d2c698c0720c0164d0459c60eb88cd701ec423ce2ce0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f73140ba9085439fb6eba5f1fd66c03b",
      "statement": "A `stockholm.Money` serializes to JSON as a single currency-suffixed string field (for example `{\"value\": \"500.00 USD\"}`), not as structured `units`/`nanos`/`currencyCode`; tests assert `payload[\"totals\"][\"cost\"][\"value\"] == \"500.00 USD\"` and that `result[\"cost\"][\"value\"]` ends with `\" CAD\"`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/routers/test_accounts.py#L92-L102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b7e3e534593b8557caaf2f29de637324c5e866825f045ed3c837088ab68df38:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/tasks/test_account.py#L95-L102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:369a8a3c2e442870122b76ca44fd6460809f30ae652f314e5853801e4bcab312:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f811f55933cc41399a7c697f95b94507",
      "statement": "Currency conversion is centralized in `PositionService._currency_convert`, which short-circuits when source and target currency codes match and otherwise calls `currency_converter.CurrencyConverter.convert(...)`, rounds to 2 decimal places, and re-wraps the result as `Money`; the `CurrencyConverter` instance is constructed once in `position_service_factory` and injected into the service.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/account/service/position.py#L257-L271",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:43abc8452ad4a193737193297a622844bbec6e06be3030f4eb131351a6dc1629:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/account/service/position.py#L339-L348",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b5bfbd5694886b2d6c296d2731652a62cc20ff2573749b5efe6f12f9e05c212:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_650f899ab59d4bb1864fb9151ea7c199",
      "statement": "Conversion is applied per position before accumulation rather than to stored values, so positions never have their `average_cost` rewritten by FX and every accumulator for total cost, total value, and total P&L adds only account-currency `Money` values.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/account/service/position.py#L179-L203",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0a22482c87b3523ce7a4da4615aeb37e7b5b00db154601a31a929c52edc9f194:"
