    {
      "id": "claim_6192175a3f1f44e59fc29b204a7e576a",
      "statement": "The frontend `Money` interface is `{ value?: string; units?: number; nanos?: number; currencyCode?: string }`, and `moneyToNumber` prefers `units + nanos / 1e9` when `units` is a number, otherwise falls back to `parseFloat(value)`, returning `0` for null, undefined, or unparseable input; `money(m)` renders `$<localized number>`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/src/lib/types/money.test.ts#L4-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:86dae18e52ff196236f2e72a5f71102ebde39f714c5b27adf1992f22cede3abe:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/src/lib/types/money.ts#L1-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:25a31f06ae4d952cfae89c93712aec77696ef47a98625a10deeb6107c4417406:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b383e5a3726642d694dc5ae1365b6c7e",
      "statement": "Because the API emits `value` strings like `\"500.00 CAD\"` with no `units`, the `units`/`nanos` branch of `moneyToNumber` is effectively unused against the live backend and real responses succeed only because `parseFloat` stops at the first non-numeric character; a serializer or parser change on either side must update both the backend shape and the frontend `Money` type together or amounts silently become wrong or `0`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/src/lib/components/accounts/accounts-list-item.svelte#L119-L123",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c11e5e205de39817f28564c74f92c1fa0ac05959d3f2633b3e689195940b8096:"
        },
